###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# MD cost is compared on a 2,048-atom fcc Cu bulk for 100 ps on one NVIDIA
# A100 80 GB GPU (LAMMPS; ASE for MatterSim-v1.0.0-1M), only in Fig. 5d:
# DP-UniAlCu is roughly two orders of magnitude faster than the universal
# models.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Table 3 errors are on the whole UniAlCu data set, which DP-UniAlCu and MACE-UniAlCu were trained on; no role is recorded because the split is not stated.
# - DPA3-OMAT is recorded under the new registry method DPA3; the DPA2 heads (MPTrj, OC2M) and MACE-MP have errors only in the SI. MatterSim-v1.0.0-5M is the registry model MatterSim-v1; the 1M variant has no registry row.
# - MACE-UniAlCu settings are in Section S3 (SI) and are not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/xu2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

